{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q19597906","formula":"C₁₃H₁₈N₂O","hill":"C13H18N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"1-methylpsilocin"},"descriptions":{"en":"1-Methylpsilocin (developmental code name CMY or CMY-16), also known as 1-methyl-4-hydroxy-N,N-dimethyltryptamine (1-Me-4-HO-DMT), is a serotonin receptor agonist and putative psychedelic drug of the tryptamine and 4-hydroxytryptamine families related to psilocin. It is the 1-methyl derivative of psilocin. The drug shows much greater selectivity as a serotonin 5-HT2C receptor agonist than psilocin, but still robustly induces psychedelic-like effects in animals, albeit with lower potency."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":44404883,"mass":218.29,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1C=C(C2=C1C=CC=C2O)CCN(C)C","inchikey":"MZZRFEIDRWKTKJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-[2-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-1-methylindol-4-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44404883","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.471,"y":-2.265,"z":-0.412,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.89,"y":1.728,"z":-0.026,"el":"N"},{"x":3.817,"y":0.306,"z":0.039,"el":"N"},{"x":0.091,"y":0.834,"z":-0.477,"el":"C"},{"x":1.519,"y":0.701,"z":-0.829,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.82,"y":-0.222,"z":-0.194,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.055,"y":0.366,"z":0.086,"el":"C"},{"x":2.406,"y":0.406,"z":0.396,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.597,"y":2.021,"z":-0.366,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.711,"y":-1.626,"z":-0.148,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.192,"y":-0.383,"z":0.411,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.923,"y":2.72,"z":0.182,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.84,"y":-2.388,"z":0.175,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.06,"y":-1.774,"z":0.45,"el":"C"},{"x":4.122,"y":-1.027,"z":-0.484,"el":"C"},{"x":4.662,"y":0.603,"z":1.196,"el":"C"},{"x":1.627,"y":-0.086,"z":-1.584,"el":"H"},{"x":1.869,"y":1.625,"z":-1.309,"el":"H"},{"x":2.062,"y":-0.485,"z":0.937,"el"